# As a-loop-whose-state-lies-in-an-environment-is-built-twice.ir, with the three in variables of a module. Each variable is asked by itself whether the typed turns write it: they write `at` alone.
# The dead zones of the three are asked in front of the loop, so no turn of the typed copy checks one. `at` is asked for an int32 there too and comes round as a parameter of the typed head; its store stays in the turn.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[at]]: {{*}} = GetModuleVariable variable=g1
# CHECK: TypeTest {{*}}testedType=i32
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: ([[round]]: i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK: Less [[round]], {{*}}form=Integers
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK: GetStringCodeUnit
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK: Increment {{*}}form=Integers
# CHECK: PutModuleVariable {{*}}variable=g1
